Phase 1 – Invoice Data Extraction to Excel (GR Automation)
Goal:
Capture invoice details from a PDF or image (PNG/JPG) and store them in an Excel file, with username & password stored only once at the top.

Technologies & Libraries
Python 3.x – Main programming language.

pdfplumber – Reads text from machine-readable PDFs.

pytesseract + Pillow – Performs OCR (Optical Character Recognition) on scanned documents and images to detect text.

os & pathlib – Handle file paths and directories.

openpyxl – Create and update Excel files.

re (Regex) – Extract structured fields like PO number, quantities, and item codes.

What is OCR?
OCR (Optical Character Recognition) is a technology that converts images of text into actual, editable text data.

This is important because scanned invoices or images are just pictures — without OCR, a computer can’t “read” them.

pytesseract is a Python wrapper for Google’s Tesseract OCR engine, which detects characters from images and converts them into text strings for further processing.

Works on JPEG, PNG, or scanned PDFs where text isn’t directly selectable.

Workflow
User uploads or drags a PDF/image file into the tool.

File type detection:

If PDF is text-based → use pdfplumber.

If PDF is scanned or an image → use pytesseract for OCR.

Extract details:

Purchase Order (PO) Number

Item Codes

Ordered Quantity

Delivered Quantity

Write to Excel:

Row 1: Username & Password (stored once, pre-filled).

Row 2 onwards: Extracted invoice details, one row per item.

Save file: Save in .xlsx format.  Append new invoice data without duplicating credentials.



System Setup for Phase 1 – Invoice Data Extraction
1. Software Requirements
•	Python 3.10 or above → Core language for automation scripts
•	PyCharm IDE (Community/Professional Edition) → Development environment
•	Tesseract OCR Engine → For extracting text from scanned invoices (PNG/PDF)
•	Microsoft Excel / LibreOffice → To open and verify extracted Excel files

2. Python Libraries
•	pytesseract → OCR text extraction
•	pdfplumber → Extract text/tables from PDF invoices
•	openpyxl → Writing extracted data into Excel files
•	pandas → Data cleaning and structuring
•	opencv-python → Preprocessing images for better OCR accuracy

3. Installation Steps
1.	Install Python 3.10 from python.org.
2.	Install PyCharm IDE (Community Edition is sufficient).
3.	Install Tesseract OCR → Add its path to system environment variables.
4.	Open PyCharm and create a new Python project.
5.	Install required libraries using terminal/command prompt
